And [the said Jacobus] obligating on these matters, in the name of our Lord King [and ourselves], generally all and singular our goods and rights, movable and immovable, present and future, and specially and expressly and by pact, all and singular the goods, revenues, and rights belonging to us and which we receive and ought to receive by whatever title, cause, or reason, by our right [in] the County of Roussillon and Cerdanya;

Concerning the aforesaid [matters] as contained in a certain letter of Illa concerning the aforesaid, [made] in the preceding months in the presence of Leonard Buge, burgess of Barcelona, according to our said letter and other [instruments], and the said contents therein, and which by pact regarding the noble [creditor] and the security;

And [the procuration] held by us made to the said Jacobus Bally, each [matter] in reason being in substance for the premises and confirmed by the present [letter], [whereby] the said Jacobus exercises procuratorial [power];

[This letter is issued] so that it may have the power to remove all matter of doubt and [all] modes [of objection] that might arise therefrom;

**By the tenor of the present [letter]**, we ratify and confirm whatever was done and promised by the said Jacobus Bally in our name, or in any manner whatsoever established and obligated, and insofar as may be desired, [we confirm it] more firmly;

Inasmuch as whatever the said Jacobus Bally promised and also obligated in our name by virtue of the aforesaid obligation — both for the observance and fulfillment of all and singular the aforesaid contents — [we] anew, for greater security, by [authority of] the present [letter], oblige generally and specially all and singular our goods and rights, movable and immovable, present and future, as is more fully contained in the said instrument of debt;

**We wish, however**, and we expressly declare that by the contents of the present [letter], our singular aforesaid obligation shall not be perpetually bound or understood [to extend] to the complete payment, satisfaction, or restitution of the quantity [beyond] that which was first confessed by the said Jacobus in our name; and that we have had and received the same for the said Jacobus in our name.

